    {
      "text": "will take sickness away from the midst of thee, Ex. 23:25 (Deut. 7:15). Lord will make … sore sicknesses, and of long continuance, Deut. 28:59. she said, He is sick, 1 Sam. 19:14. whatsoever plague, whatsoever sickness there be, 1 Kgs. 8:37. son … fell sick … and his sickness was so sore, 1 Kgs. 17:17. was Hezekiah sick, 2 Kgs. 20:1 (2 Chr. 32:24; Isa. 38:1). countenance sad, seeing thou art not sick, Neh. 2:2. when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth, Ps. 35:13. make all his bed in his sickness, Ps. 41:3. Hope deferred maketh the heart sick, Prov. 13:12. stricken me … and I was not sick, Prov. 23:35. whole head is sick, Isa. 1:5. inhabitant shall not say, I am sick, Isa. 33:24. neither have ye healed that which was sick, Ezek. 34:4. will strengthen that which was sick, Ezek. 34:16. ye offer the lame and sick, Mal. 1:8.",
